# Alacritty Tab Management Implementation

## Overview
This codebase implements in-window tab functionality for Alacritty on Linux with comprehensive tab management including creation, switching, closing, and visual rendering.

## Key Architecture

### Platform-Specific Implementation
- **macOS**: Uses native window tabbing APIs (unchanged)
- **Linux**: In-window tab system with tab bar UI and multiple terminal instances
- **Other platforms**: Creates separate windows (unchanged)

### Core Data Structures
```rust
// Tab management (Linux only)
pub struct TabManager {
    pub tabs: Vec<TabInfo>,
    pub active_tab: usize,
}

pub struct TabInfo {
    pub terminal: Arc<FairMutex<Term<EventProxy>>>,
    pub title: String,
    pub master_fd: RawFd,
    pub shell_pid: u32,
}
```

